   "subject": "Re: legend for geom_errorbar",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Giovanni,\r<br>\r<br>I know it&#39;s frustrating when you don&#39;t receive a reply straight away,\r<br>but posting your question in multiple places just makes more work for\r<br>those of us who want to help you.  In the future, please post your\r<br>query once on one mailing list, and then wait for a decent amount of\r<br>time.  I&#39;m a busy guy and I can&#39;t guarantee that I&#39;ll get to your\r<br>problems as soon as you post them.\r<br>\r<br>Hadley\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sun, May 2, 2010 at 9:07 AM, Giovanni Azua &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brav...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; I need to plot multiple CIs and compare them ... I manage to do so with a\r<br>&gt; code similar to the example included below. However, I could not find any\r<br>&gt; way to add a Legend to indicate which CI corresponds to which method ... can\r<br>&gt; anyone please advise?\r<br>&gt; Many thanks in advance,\r<br>&gt; Best regards,\r<br>&gt; Giovanni\r<br>&gt; rm(list=ls())                                              # clear workspace\r<br>&gt; library(ggplot2)                                           # use ggplot2\r<br>&gt; library\r<br>&gt; methodlabels &lt;- c(&quot;Classic&quot;, &quot;Own Bootstrap&quot;,              # prepare plot\r<br>&gt; labels\r<br>&gt; &quot;R Bootstrap&quot;)\r<br>&gt; errortypelabels &lt;- c(&quot;&#39;Normal&#39;&quot;, &quot;&#39;Student-t&#39;&quot;,            # prepare plot\r<br>&gt; labels\r<br>&gt; &quot;&#39;Exponential&#39;&quot;)\r<br>&gt; betalabels &lt;- c(&quot;&#39;Beta_1&#39;&quot;, &quot;&#39;Beta_2&#39;&quot;, &quot;&#39;Beta_3&#39;&quot;)        # prepare plot\r<br>&gt; labels\r<br>&gt; betas &lt;- c(1, -2, 3)                                       # my real\r<br>&gt; parameters\r<br>&gt; set.seed(11)\r<br>&gt; S &lt;- 100\r<br>&gt; B &lt;- 50\r<br>&gt; P &lt;- length(betas)\r<br>&gt; classiccis &lt;- owncis &lt;- rbootcis &lt;- array(data=0,dim=c(S,1,3,2))\r<br>&gt; for (p in 1:P) {\r<br>&gt; classiccis[,1,p,1] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]-1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; classiccis[,1,p,2] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]+1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; owncis[,1,p,1] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]-1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; owncis[,1,p,2] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]+1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; rbootcis[,1,p,1] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]-1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; rbootcis[,1,p,2] &lt;- rnorm(100,mean=betas[p]+1.0,sd=0.5)\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; ##\r<br>&gt; ## Function that generates the ggplot of the CI for a given parameter\r<br>&gt; ## and error type\r<br>&gt; ##\r<br>&gt; ciplot &lt;- function() {\r<br>&gt; x &lt;- 1:S\r<br>&gt; y &lt;- rep(betas[p],S)\r<br>&gt; data &lt;- data.frame(x,y)\r<br>&gt; classiclimits &lt;- aes(x=x[1:100],ymax = classiccis[1:100,e,p,1],\r<br>&gt; ymin=classiccis[1:100,e,p,2])\r<br>&gt; ownlimits &lt;- aes(x=x[1:100]+0.4,ymax = owncis[1:100,e,p,1],\r<br>&gt; ymin=owncis[1:100,e,p,2])\r<br>&gt; rbootlimits &lt;- aes(x=x[1:100]+0.8,ymax = rbootcis[1:100,e,p,1],\r<br>&gt; ymin=rbootcis[1:100,e,p,2])\r<br>&gt; g1 &lt;- ggplot(data, aes(x=x, y=y))\r<br>&gt; g1 + geom_errorbar(classiclimits, colour=&quot;red&quot;) + geom_errorbar(\r<br>&gt;      ownlimits, colour=&quot;green&quot;) + geom_errorbar(rbootlimits,\r<br>&gt;      colour=&quot;blue&quot;) + geom_hline(yintercept = betas[p]) + xlab(\r<br>&gt;      &quot;Simulation&quot;) + ylab(betalabels[p]) + opts(title = paste(&quot;CI for&quot;,\r<br>&gt;      errortypelabels[e],&quot;error, &quot;,betalabels[p],&quot;,&quot;,S/5,\r<br>&gt;      &quot;simulations and &quot;,B,&quot;bootstrapped samples&quot;))\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; ##\r<br>&gt; ## Execute one by one ... note they have to be global\r<br>&gt; ## otherwise seems that ggplot won&#39;t find them.\r<br>&gt; ##\r<br>&gt; ## p - means parameter index\r<br>&gt; ## e - means error type index\r<br>&gt; ##\r<br>&gt; p=1;e=1;ciplot()\r<br>&gt; p=2;e=1;ciplot()\r<br>&gt; p=3;e=1;ciplot()\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing\r<br>&gt; list.\r<br>&gt; Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383536171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hzp2u9u4ScVMKJ3-tLb02\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383536171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DuSegZXbBIjNfHxKdb-pF\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "-- \r<br>Assistant Professor / Dobelman Family Junior Chair\r<br>Department of Statistics / Rice University\r<br><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383536171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1un6_3lsdfEijgWLEqRK2v\">http://had.co.nz/</a>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>-- \r<br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.\r<br>Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383536171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hzp2u9u4ScVMKJ3-tLb02\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a>\r<br>\r<br>To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383536171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DuSegZXbBIjNfHxKdb-pF\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
